    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup for May 29th is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who sits at a clear tier-leading 74.98 efficiency score. Despite facing a left-hander, his elite pedigree and second-spot placement in the order neutralize matchup concerns, making him our primary engine for R and RBI today. Following closely behind are **Matt Chapman** (69.74) and **Luis Arraez** (69.53), both of whom benefit significantly from the favorable park factors and the 4.24 xERA provided by the opposing starter, Lorenzen. **Jung Hoo Lee** (67.72) also capitalizes on this same matchup, as his strong platoon edge against right-handed pitching elevates his value to a top-tier start. While we are aggressively targeting the soft pitching matchup in that contest, **Taylor Ward** remains a focal point; despite a daunting 2.80 xERA matchup against Macko, his prime leadoff role and park-adjusted upside push his efficiency to 59.22, validating his start in the OF5 slot.\n\nThe toughest decision at the back end of the roster involved **Bryson Stott**, who narrowly missed the starting nine with a 42.91 score. While his 85% SB-friendly sprint speed against a slower pitcher was a compelling incentive, the downward pressure from the opposing left-handed starter and a lower raw efficiency projection ultimately relegated him to the bench in favor of higher-floor assets like **Jonathan Aranda**, who enjoys a massive boost from a +12% dynamic platoon advantage. Caution is warranted elsewhere: **Will Smith** faces the stiffest test of the day against Wheeler\u2019s 2.86 xERA, leading to a marginal 43.58 score. Similarly, **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Gavin Sheets** are priced as mid-tier starts (45.64 and 48.60, respectively) due to the presence of elite arm talent on the mound. We continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz**, who remain on the IL, while **Lawrence Butler**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Drew Gilbert** are excluded from today\u2019s active rotation to preserve our game cap efficiency.",
